 "description": "Wan2020 - risk estimation and prediction of the transmission of COVID-19 in maninland China excluding Hubei province\nBioModels BIOMD0000000981 (curated). SBML file: Wan2020.xml.\nSimulation: 0 to 80 time units (SED-ML: Wan2020.sedml), sampling 1.\nRun switches: -ig:mass -INT:1 -obeymaxint\nVerification against libRoadRunner (SBML reference): PASS, max |difference| = 4.27e-06 of species peak (worst: Recovered_from_hospitals)\nSBML time units are used unchanged as Kintecus seconds.\nConversion notes:\n  [info] species 'Total_population' is defined by an assignment rule; not a Kintecus state (not output)\n  [info] Susceptible_to_Exposed term 1/2: rate is not proportional to its reactants; divided form used with 1/(c+1e-30) so an empty species is not consumed\n  [info] Susceptible_to_Exposed term 2/2: rate is not proportional to its reactants; divided form used with 1/(c+1e-30) so an empty species is not consumed\n  [info] Susceptible_to_isolated term 1/2: rate is not proportional to its reactants; divided form used with 1/(c+1e-30) so an empty species is not consumed\n  [info] Susceptible_to_isolated term 2/2: rate is not proportional to its reactants; divided form used with 1/(c+1e-30) so an empty species is not consumed\n  [info] Exposed_to_Quarantined term 1/2: rate is not proportional to its reactants; divided form used with 1/(c+1e-30) so an empty species is not consumed\n  [info] Exposed_to_Quarantined term 2/2: rate is not proportional to its reactants; divided form used with 1/(c+1e-30) so an empty species is not consumed\n  [info] Infected_to_Quarantined term 1/2: rate is not proportional to its reactants; divided form used with 1/(c+1e-30) so an empty species is not consumed\n  [info] Infected_to_Quarantined term 2/2: rate is not proportional to its reactants; divided form used with 1/(c+1e-30) so an empty species is not consumed\n  [info] Asymptomatic_to_Quarantined term 1/2: rate is not proportional to its reactants; divided form used with